  "findings": [
    "Cross-track fixed-margin results: 81/130 matched within 50 ms, 49 missed, 42 extras, versus 103/27/50 for unchanged v5. No threshold was tuned to repair the result.",
    "The rejected correct kicks often match another song\u2019s bass-heavy mix slightly better than a kick reference. The dictionary and representation do not provide reliable class identity across these mixtures.",
    "No global lower-margin rejection boundary can reject any wider-unmatched baseline event while preserving all 103 current tight matches in this development set. This optimistic label-informed bound is not a deployable threshold.",
    "At label-guided +20/+35/+50 ms endpoints the same model accepts 114/128/117 of 130 kick labels. That is oracle classification, not detector recall or proof that 35 ms is an optimal delay.",
    "Late Night accepts 45/53 negative events in its reviewed kick-free passage, including baseline and failed-hybrid event times; Midnight accepts 1/11. These secondary negative probes are distinct from headline baseline extras and must not be added to them.",
    "Timing matters: Bad Guy accepts 12/15 labels at +20 ms, 15/15 at +35 ms, but only 7/15 at +50 ms. Waiting longer is not a demonstrated general solution for this fixed fingerprint.",
    "This rejects the particular coarse whole-mixture spectral-template method and reference pack, not all non-neural timbre recognition. Source separation leakage, mixture context, reference diversity and event-age mismatch remain limitations."
